STEP 1 — characterize coex BEFORE the fix (BT-local lock only)
--------------------------------------------------------------
Boot: BT up over WHD bus at 3.3s (patchram), then
   [14172] whd_wifi_join failed checkres=33555457
   <err> infineon_airoc_wifi: Failed to connect with network
=> WiFi association FAILS whenever the BT poll thread is active. In W2 (BT off)
   WiFi associated cleanly (192.168.4.28). Root cause: the BT path drove gSPI
   backplane transfers with a BT-LOCAL lock, unserialized against WHD's WLAN
   bus thread (airoc_whd_hal_spi.c has no mutex). This is the REFERENCE §2.7
   concurrent-bus corruption — here it manifests as a failed WLAN join rather
   than a kernel panic, because cybt's reads now route through WHD's
   F1-overflow-aware backplane path (so NO assert/panic: 0 faults).
Soak (3 cyc bounded, results/w4_whd_coex_soak_3cyc_20260619.log):
   cycles:3 faults:0  total notifications:0  (no coex established)

STEP 2 — the W6 fix: shared gSPI bus lock
-----------------------------------------
A single recursive mutex now serializes ALL gSPI access:
 - WHD WLAN: durable patch brackets whd_bus_spi_transfer() (incl. the
   SPI_DATA_IRQ_SHARED pinctrl/IRQ toggle) — patches/airoc_whd_hal_spi_shared_bus_lock.patch
 - BT: whd_bt_glue.c cyw43_thread_enter/exit -> whd_bus_lock/unlock (held across
   each cybt read-modify-write sequence). Strong def in whd_transport.c.
Boot AFTER the fix:
   3.3s whd_bt_glue: BT up over WHD bus (patchram loaded)
   "Connected"  (WiFi ASSOCIATED with BT active — previously failed)
   ble_peripheral: Bluetooth initialized; starting advertising
=> DEVICE-SIDE COEXISTENCE FIXED: WiFi + BT both up, 0 faults. The §2.7
   contention that broke WLAN association is resolved.
Soak (4 cyc bounded, results/w4w6_whd_coex_soak_4cyc_20260619.log):
   cycles:4 faults:0  (no crash) BUT total notifications:0

REMAINING BLOCKER (next): BLE not discoverable over-air
-------------------------------------------------------
Host BleakScanner.discover finds 6 BLE devices but NOT test-picow-bluetooth;
ble_central.py -> "peripheral not found in scan". The device logs advertising
with no error, but no ADV_IND is seen over-air, so the bleak central never
connects (0 notifications). This is an HCI-level issue independent of the bus
contention just fixed (candidates: HCI command-complete/event delivery during
the advertising-setup sequence via the 4 ms BT RX poll; advertising
params/data; BT TX-under-coex). Must be resolved before the coex soak can hit
its notification baseline. W4 (parity soak) and W6 (2 h zero-fault gate) remain
IN-PROGRESS pending this.

NET: W6 shared-bus-lock fix = verified-good for the device-side §2.7 contention
